Z||000000||DJRice||08-03-2000||07:15 PM||||Well I wandered into the local boneyard a couple of saturdays ago and came out with the shift boot and handle from a 99 Pontiac Grand Am.  The shifter fits on perfectly but I didnt want to cut my shift boot and the Grand am shift boot required a bit of modification to fit.  Basically I to cut the base in half and strecth it to fit over the opening in the console.<P>Anyway, here are the picks, tell me what you think...<P>Before:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stock_auto_shifter.jpg">  <BR>After: <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Grand_am_shifter1.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grand_am_shifter2.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"<p>[This message has been edited by DJRice (edited 08-03-2000).]||||reg||1
